<title>USA: Two Massachusetts towns part company on bond acts.</title>
<headline>Two Massachusetts towns part company on bond acts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Massachusetts voters reacted differently in two towns, with Needham approving a local bond issue and Dover rejecting one, local officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Needham: winning margin, 8,678 versus 6,562 against. Approved issuing bonds not to exceed $5.75 miln for extraordinary repairs and additions to the Newman School Building that would be exempt.</p>
<p>Dover: losing margin, 1,437 versus 1,208 for. Rejected issuing bonds for a new town garage and site improvements at 2 Dedham Street that would be exempt.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
